!! Vitals

* ''Branch'' `feature/lararium-node-5`, ahead of `origin` — `git rev-list --count origin/feature/lararium-node-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits; the operator pushes. Dirt in the tree that no lane authored: the `mempalace` and `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` submodule pointers, `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`. Never commit, stash, or revert those.
* ''Landed in the last sign-off'' (CHANGELOG `[Unreleased]`, the SIGN-OFF BATCH lines): the gate-signed `lar:auth-ok`; `lar:session` frames on an admitted socket; leaf↔leaf proof as a library; the PersonaGroup ring on both vessels through one function; the oracle crossing only to a proven peer over the gated `/oracle` socket, every HTTP path the one `CLOSED_DOOR`; `/api/health` on a lararium alone; the `hosted` invite arm and its countersign over the live session; R1 (one file, one carrier; `MemeStreamParser` gone); the carrier grammar's name-matched ahu pairing and the `ahu-pair-parity` weld; bag doors refusing a torn frame; one presenter, forks per board, findings surfaced; `rite quorum` and `needsQuorum`; the Codex hold closed and the hearths gate quiet unless held; the offering replication suite; the browser share config reading the armed gate.
* ''E2E'' (the whole staged set): 29 of 29 files — 208 passed, 1 expected fail.
* ''The witness fleet'' (`tools/witness-all.sh`, what CI runs) ends on a verdict table, one line per witness with its own exit code — count the reds there, never in the transcript. 33 of 33 read ok. Each dist-reading witness refuses a stale build by name (exit 2) — rebuild the named package, run `node tools/stamp-build.mjs . --pkg <name>`, re-run; a comment edit in a package's `src/` stales its dist too. CI's witnesses job also runs every `tools/*.test.mjs` (12 files, 46 tests).
* ''Typecheck'' (`tools/typecheck-witness.sh`): every package clean across 11 projects.
* ''Unit suites'': `lararium-tw5` 1732; `lararium-mesh` 2459; `lararium-node` 1400; `lares-cli` 554; `lararium-keyhive` 146; `lararium-browser` 145; `lararium-web` 9; `lararium-memetic-frame` 357; `lararium-sensorium` 952 Python + 54 vitest. The tree-sitter carrier grammar reads clean.
* ''HEADS-UP — the operator's live `~/.lares` vessel'': its stored device edges were signed over the clocked layout, and any rotated seal lineage it holds carries no signed rolls. Both fail verification on this build. Do NOT stand that vessel on this build; it needs the re-found or a re-mint.
* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): the last run read a pushed head behind the local tree — `gh run list --branch feature/lararium-node-5` names it. The next push is the witness for everything since.
* ''Known environmental reds'': `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` fail when a browser or server socket is missing.

