<<~ ahu #/wounds>>

!! Open wounds, ranked

The round-5 sign-off accepted every lane but one finding: F1, on the hosted countersign, whose fix is in flight. No other operator ruling is pending.

# ''THE RE-FOUND, one act'' (rulings: the operator's STABLE and CUSTODY rulings; canon `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu`, `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine`). It mints unversioned names, re-mints the engine and edge, and re-seats the Nexus — never a persona or sealed-body wipe; DESTROY-class strings stay frozen.
## ''STABLE — the founding state.''
### One interactive founding act, under one passphrase, produces the place, persona zero, a private charter (a cabal-of-one: one seat, t=1, per-seat next digests) and the keyring keyed by `epochCid`, minted at the seat, never at boot.
### Every Nexus has a charter; guests walk the private Nexus, their planes persona-scoped.
### Boards resolve per relation (`nexusIdentity` returns one island today).
### Every leaf keeps its own floor root, with its own slot beside the group face (a two-mount shape).
### Add-a-face (A): the daemon writes the public half, the terminal seals the recovery share, seating stays a separate act.
### Delete the bare primary-path seal import.
### The mirror guard keys on posture.
### The direct-store verbs (`publish`, device-admit, `persona new N`) route through the live daemon over UDS. This carries the crew's live-holder gap: a direct-store write beside a live holder lands on disk the holder never carries.
## ''CUSTODY — the Vessel KEK.''
### One VK seals every carrier: archives, shares, the persona root, the next-root seed and the custody root.
### LUKS-style keyslots of Clevis `sss` trees, with pins passphrase · paper · ember · tpm; a BACKUP route (passphrase or paper) is required at every tier, and bind refuses a tree without one.
### EMBER: Tang-shaped, per-relation, holding no share of VK. The locality law: an unattended ember answers on the local link only; a relay pin must be attended.
### The vessel rests at the floor, then the ember raise, which lapses by non-renewal. HOT ⊥ COLD: VK and keyhive state stay hot; the root, recovery shares and next seed unwrap per act.
### The floor key keeps the public name ⊥ the sealed custody root derives the veil.
### `unbind` offers a VK rotation loudly, every time.
### `vault unlock|bind|unbind|status` over UDS; `LARES_ARCHIVE_PASSPHRASE` retires.
### The cleartext vessel seed, persona root and next-root seed get wrapped.
### Hardware x-only ECDH measurement: deferred.
## ''CARRIED into the re-found.'' The per-Nexus wire key (it also cuts the oracle pointer's vessel-key correlation, `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/pronaos#/the-rung-ladder`); per-seat `nextKeyDigests`; S1, a multi-vessel kahu quorum; L1, the realm root map from `keptBy`; the coal-only seed without `schemaVersion`; the cadence inception (t/k); the sentinel re-key; the chairs re-keyed to per-Nexus leaves, which un-owes the invite's `seat` arm; `waking-floor-announce` (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-announcement`). Then the island `schema_version` (~35 files) drops its counter.
# ''ROUND 6.''
## ''The proof-first / silence protocol lane'' (Noise IK shape): the dialer proves first and a stranger draws silence. It covers the gate's `lar:challenge` naming the vessel key to any opener, the oracle route answering distinguishably, and N8: the membership relay's unsigned second handshake collapses onto the auth wire.
## ''Leaf↔leaf transport'' (N2): Automerge sync between leaves through a herm, with `leaf-peer-proof` bound to the session it admits (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/identity-slot-policy#/the-leaf-taxonomy`).
## ''The held-out dispatch needs'': a host-built dist, and `vessel found` on the runner.

''Carried, unranked''
* Road (iv): surface-for-review.
* Q6: loans keyed by CID.
* A design call on `/cas` timing; whether the parallel-draft alert persists.
* `packages/lararium-sensorium/requirements.txt` calls the tree-sitter versions one (Python binding 0.26, CLI 0.27; both ABI 15).

''Pending operator rulings''
* None standing, beyond any ruling F1 asks for.

''Needs the operator''
* ''Grammar submissions'': whether the Nexus Kahu or the corpus-kahu receive them.
* ''The offering's `offer`/`witness` caps'' against the Lamplighter stack.
* ''Engine cadence, still open'' (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu` `#/contract`): who holds a cadence share; one daemon hosting two engine epochs; whether partial conformance lands before `kahuli engine` un-holds.
* ''Backstop seam (b), PHASE 5'' (`tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`): three child-edit shapes the test marks as the operator's call.
* ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`'s header): `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph` (canon memes pin their mesh `source-file`), `pronaos`, `offering-inspection` (own mesh-namespace memes). Each moves or stays only by ruling.
* ''The capture cell'' sits isolated for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/`, `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`, the sensorium-machina S5 ruling) places capture in Python per stream with the TS @daemon coordinating only; the TS cell carries the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.
* ''The tree's git config'': restore `core.bare = false` (operator's hand only).

''Deferred by law or by the operator''
* ''The Sensorium's logic'' (`packages/lararium-sensorium/**`, tw5 `form-layer/**`, mesh `ffz-project`, `clock-recovery`, coupling/metric modules): the measure-servo aliases in `ffz-project.ts`, one five-band ladder (Title case `ApertureBand`, the others derived), the `lar_feedback` output field name. Frames inside it stay in scope for healing at any time.
* ''Tangle, the putback law, the tongue fold'' — gated on a real return trip and a whole regeneration of `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext` (mirror pairing, round-trip CI, Markdown injection into `hana`). The aka/weave rhyme (`memetic-wikitext-framing.mem` Annex) waits on tangle.
* ''A relay-stream profile'' — a stream of carriers belongs to the SYN-framed profile (`&#x0016;`, held in reserve); one `.mem` file frames one carrier. The profile defines batch framing and resynchronisation.
* ''A carrier seal'' — re-mint an attestation mark with a computed, verified check when signing lands.
* ''EOT targeting'' — what a resolved `-> to=` would name (the declared-unresolved meaning stands).
* ''A standing whole-tree gate'' (build every package from clean, run every witness and suite) — run as a spirit pass, not built into the CLI or a trigger.

